    "derivation": "elite_cs66.a1_stand/provenance/step_derivation.json",
    "notes": "A1 STEP supplies the stand, CAD arm mount positions and table pose; catalog CS66 arms and worktable are reused. The stand is rotated 180 degrees about world Z The table is later centered laterally on the rotated CAD column per the 2026-10-08 request; see table_centering. After that rotation, the controller left/right arms attach to the CAD right/left mount frames respectively. Local Z corrections of +90/-90 degrees align the assembled base rotations with this bench's LeRobot left/right_world_rotation matrices. The assembly keeps the official CS66 joint coordinates. Recipe start positions are optional states in config/start_pose.json; they are not baked into joint origins or limits. Add two unchanged official DH AG95 grippers directly at CS66 flanges per user-confirmed matching four bolt holes. Rotate AG95 local X opening axis onto the TacCap reference local Y opening axis; no adapter and no copied mechanical parameters.",
